**UI changes in the `memories-panel__actions` div (lines 73-82):**

Add a search icon button next to the existing "view file" button:

```tsx
<div className="memories-panel__actions">
  <button className="memories-panel__action-btn" onClick={handleViewFile} title={t('viewMemoryFile')} aria-label={t('viewMemoryFile')}>
    {/* existing file SVG */}
  </button>
  <button
    className={`memories-panel__action-btn${searchOpen ? ' memories-panel__action-btn--active' : ''}`}
    onClick={() => {
      setSearchOpen((prev) => !prev);
      if (searchOpen) setSearchTerm('');
    }}
    title={t('searchMemories')}
    aria-label={t('searchMemories')}
  >
    <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokeWidth="2" strokeLinecap="round" strokeLinejoin="round">
      <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8" />
      <line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65" />
    </svg>
  </button>
</div>
```

**Search input (insert between actions div and the grouped sections):**

```tsx
{searchOpen && (
  <input
    className="memories-panel__search-input"
    type="text"
    placeholder={t('searchMemoriesPlaceholder')}
    value={searchTerm}
    onChange={(e) => setSearchTerm(e.target.value)}
    autoFocus
  />
)}
```

**Filter logic:**

The Memories tab has a grouped structure. The filtering should operate on the underlying `entries` array, and the grouping should be computed from the filtered entries. Add `useMemo` to the React import, then restructure the `grouped` computation (currently at line 68-69):

```typescript
const filteredEntries = useMemo(() => {
  if (!searchTerm) return entries;
  const term = searchTerm.toLowerCase();
  return entries.filter((entry) => entry.content.toLowerCase().includes(term));
}, [entries, searchTerm]);

const grouped = CATEGORY_ORDER.map((cat) => ({
  category: cat,
  items: filteredEntries.filter((e) => e.category === cat),
}));
```

**Rendering changes:**
- The existing `grouped.map(...)` loop at lines 83-104 will automatically show only matching entries per category, since `grouped` is now derived from `filteredEntries`.
- Categories with no matching entries will show their existing "No preferences/facts/patterns saved yet" empty message, which is acceptable behavior.
- Optionally, add a "no results" message when `searchTerm && filteredEntries.length === 0`.

**Hide search button when no entries exist:** Only show the search button when `entries.length > 0`, to avoid showing a search toggle when there is nothing to search.

---

### Step 5: Add CSS Styles

**Files to modify:**
- `/Users/cyyeh/Desktop/duckdb-data-agent/frontend/src/components/Sidebar.css`
- `/Users/cyyeh/Desktop/duckdb-data-agent/frontend/src/components/SkillsPanel.css`
- `/Users/cyyeh/Desktop/duckdb-data-agent/frontend/src/components/MemoriesPanel.css`

**Shared search input pattern (replicated per component, following the BEM convention of each component owning its CSS):**

The search input style is modeled after the existing `results-table__global-search` pattern. Each component gets its own BEM class.

